9c6d1734351843a7eac8850.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a6bd3960c2bcb774c9c6d1734351843a7eac8850.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued September 14 at 6:47PM MDT until September 14 at 8:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"FFWGJT\n\nThe National Weather Service in Grand Junction has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nWest Central Archuleta County in southwestern Colorado...\nSoutheastern La Plata County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* Until 800 PM MDT.\n\n* At 647 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or\nexpected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nBayfield, Ignacio, Oxford, Falfa, Bondad, Chimney Rock and\nLonetree.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nSan Juan River, Beaver Creek, Heflin Creek, Indian Creek, Hayden\nCreek, Salt Creek, West Fork Devil Creek, Animas River, Cat Creek,\nDry Creek, Rock Creek, Florida River, Ignacio Creek, Dudley Creek,\nSheep Creek, Pinos River, Los, Piedra River, Elk Creek, Round\nMeadow Creek, Squaw Creek, Spring Creek, Devil Creek, Stollsteimer\nCreek, Archuleta Creek, Yellowjacket Creek, Crowbar Creek, Ute\nCreek and Freeman Creek.","ends":"2026-09-14T20:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.da15216bad9a7c185c829c94e2021b908b62bb43.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.da15216bad9a7c185c829c94e2021b908b62bb43.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-14T23:32:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 142332 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Servic